A||||3||Adrift||Alarm Installation - Help!||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-26-2001||03:52 PM||||First quick question: do all the wires needed for an alarm installation run through the center console?  I was thinking of rather then splice to the wires right under steering wheel where theieves always look splice into it under the centre console, would be bullet proof!<P>So I'm trying to install an alarm (Audiovox Dps-410) in my car. I have never installed an alarm before. I have my trusty haynes manual in one hand, and the alarm installation manual in other, and im still stumped. For example, the first wire I need to find is the +12 VDC Constant Battery Source. I open up my Haynes, turn to the wiring section, and am lost. Can Anyone point me in the right direction? I can't afford to shell out the $100 for installation, and would like to learn more about the electronics anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex2004||11-26-2001||04:29 PM||||All of the wire's EXCEPT the lock and unlock wires can be found by the ecm.  You can connect your 12v constant to yuor fuse box constant, just check it with a test light. You could hide your module (alarm box) ontop  or beside your radio if the is small enough, or on top of the radio if you have a single din radio. here is a link bulldog security's website to the wire diagram for fiero's  and i used this when i installed my alarm.  Hope this helps.  <A HREF="http://www.bulldogsecurity.com/wires/fiero84-88.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bulldogsecurity.com/wires/fiero84-88.htm</A> <BR>Alex...<BR> <BR> <BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-26-2001||07:21 PM||||In the installation manual it says to look for the "300Ma GROUND OUTPUT WHEN ARMED -N.C&gt; STARTER DISABLE (Optional Relay Required) and 300MA GROUND OUTPUT WHEN DISARMED N. O. STRATER DISABLE (Optional Relay Required)...<BR>I wasn't provided with any type of relay when I bought the alarm... do I have to buy one in order to allow the alarm to disable the start? What type do I have to buy?<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-26-2001||07:22 PM||||OK first, Places to put the alarm box are:<BR>Under the radio in the console<BR>On the right had side of the console in the "pocket" where the factory sub amp would be. (If your car doesn't have the factory sub)<BR>Above any of the vents under the front dash. This usually requires removing the top of the dash. It's hard to see and a pain to get at. If it's hard for you to get to it is twice as hard for the thief.<P>Next, Always solder your connections so you don'y have to worry about intermittenet connections later.<P>Finally, Pull down the fuse holder. On the bottom Edge you will see terminals marked "BATT" and "ACC".<BR>The "BATT" is constant power from the battery. Splice into the wires behind. I usually follow it to where it joins into the main harness wrap. Then after you splice in, re-wrap it so it looks stock.<BR>The "ACC" is the switched power.<BR>Always splice into the wires behind. That way the connections won't be "in sight" of a potential thief. <P>Relay's are available at Radio Shack for $2.99. Just get a heavy duty 30A.<BR>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
